### 2026-09-08 — V5 rulebook sync, Phase 1 (Mastery + Subtype data fix)

The tabletop rulebook was revised to "V5" (a new source docx converted to markdown, then merged
into the rules-reference site at `COFC-Coaching/essence-system`'s
`artifacts/essence-system/src/content/rules/`, and mirrored into this repo's GitHub wiki for
dev/build reference — see the wiki's Home page). A code audit against the updated rules found the
Influence system, Tier/Level progression, and the Armory(8)/Signature Equipment(4) equipment split
were **already implemented** in `actor-combatant.mjs`/`item-card.mjs`, closer to canon than
expected — the real gaps were narrower. This session did the two smallest, lowest-risk items from
that audit's Phase 1:

1. **Mastery**, previously entirely unimplemented (zero code hits). Added `hasMastery(cardSystem,
   actorExpertises)` in `utils.mjs`: a card's `system.expertises` (comma-separated names) plus
   `system.expertisesMode` (`"any"` = requires 1, `"any2"` = requires 2) already existed as data
   but were never read anywhere. Mastery applies when the rolling actor's `system.expertises`
   contains MORE of the card's listed names than the required count — flat +1 Surge, non-stacking,
   per the rules text. Wired into `rollEssencePool` (`essence-roll.mjs`) via a new `bonusSurges`
   param that adds to `combat.surges` before it's stored in the chat message's
   `surgesAvailable` flag, so the existing click-to-spend Surge flow needed no changes. Both
   `actor-sheet.mjs` and `npc-sheet.mjs`'s `#onRollItem` call it identically (yet more of the
   known sheet-duplication debt in item #2 above — not fixed here, consistent with that being
   accepted debt rather than blocking work).
2. **`SUBTYPE_DATABASE` data fix** in `expertise-database.mjs`. This table was never actually wired
   to any UI (`EXPERTISE_DATABASE` is used by the wizard/sheet; `SUBTYPE_DATABASE` has zero
   importers) — so this was reference-data correction, not a live bug. Diffed all 9 skills against
   the rulebook's new Appendix A (Combat Skill Reference): Prowess, Ballistics, Gestalt, Cunning,
   Psionics, Leadership, Ritualism, and Calling all had wrong and/or missing Subtype names (e.g.
   Prowess was missing "Chain"/"Maneuver" and listed a nonexistent "Guard"; Calling had 8 entries,
   several not in canon, instead of the correct 7). Magecraft was already correct. Left the shared
   "Reaction" 8th-subtype (every skill's universal Reaction slot) out of the per-skill arrays,
   matching the table's pre-existing convention.

