need real Action-instance objects and declare/resolve-reverse-order sequencing this system has
never modeled — closer to a Phase 3-sized build than a quick fix). Added
`playState.lastReactionRound`/`lastReactionCombatantId` to `actor-combatant.mjs`; using a Reaction
Card records the current Combat round + whose Turn is active, and warns (never blocks) if the same
actor tries another Reaction while that same Turn is still the active one. This is explicitly an
approximate proxy for "one Reaction per Action," not a real per-trigger check — the warning text
says so, and both the schema comment and this entry exist so nobody later mistakes it for full
enforcement and builds on top of a false assumption.

