### 2026-09-19 -- Pre-release audit caught a real content-loss bug: 5 Consumable Kits silently deleted

Before cutting the v0.7.1 release (the /cut-release skill's own working-tree check), reviewed the
full uncommitted diff by hand rather than committing it blind. Found 14 deleted `packs/_source`
files. Nine were already-documented, correct exclusions (the 7 garbled Neon "Basic" rows Phase 7's
own build-history entry explains, plus the old pre-fix Burning/Dazed condition rows Phase 3/5
replaced) -- verified against their citing comments in build-packs.mjs and confirmed legitimate.

The other five were not: Medical Pack, Explorer's Kit, Explosives Pack, Munitions Pack, and Potion
Pack (all Consumable Kit / Toolkit equipment) had no replacement anywhere in the diff, and grepping
for their names across every current source file (component-catalog-data.json,
extra-equipment-data.json, even at the last released commit) turned up nothing -- they predated the
current equipment-generation pipeline entirely, as orphaned legacy `packs/_source` files with no
JSON source counterpart. 0.7.0 was this sync's first-ever *unscoped* `build-packs.mjs` run (every
prior phase used `--only=`); the unscoped path clears the whole `packs/_source` directory before
regenerating (see the `fs.rmSync(SOURCE_DIR, ...)` at the top of `main()`), so anything with no
source data to regenerate from was silently dropped as collateral damage. The 0.7.0 session's own
report had verified Neon's `equipment_cards` table being empty was "expected, not a stale-cache
wipe" -- true as far as it went, but it didn't check whether the full-directory clear also ate
files with no source-data counterpart at all, which is exactly what happened here.

Fixed by adding all five as proper hand-authored entries to `extra-equipment-data.json` (matching
the existing Toolkit/Consumable-Kit entries' shape, `uses` field included) rather than trying to
resurrect the old `_source` files directly -- they need to survive the next unscoped rebuild, not
just this one. Re-ran `node scripts/build-packs.mjs --only=equipment`: 89 -> 94 equipment items,
JSON valid, no other packs touched. Folded into the still-uncommitted 0.7.1 CHANGELOG entry rather
than minting a new version, since nothing has shipped yet.

Lesson for future unscoped rebuilds: `--only=`-scoped rebuilds (every phase before 0.7.0 used them)
can't surface this class of bug, because they only ever touch the one pack directory named -- an
orphaned legacy file in a *different* pack directory just sits there untouched, silently surviving
right up until the first time someone runs a full rebuild. The first unscoped run after a long
scoped-only stretch is exactly when to expect this and check for it, the way this session did by
reading the full `git status` deletion list by hand rather than trusting row-count comparisons
alone (row counts went up, not down, once the fix landed -- a straightforward "did the count drop"
check would have caught this immediately, and should be standard practice after any unscoped
rebuild going forward).
